---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const skills = [
  { area: 'Programming & Data', items: 'Python (pandas, NumPy, Pyomo), MATLAB/Simulink, Git, Excel, LaTeX' },
  {
    area: 'Optimization & Analytics',
    items: 'Mixed-integer linear programming, multi-stage stochastic optimization, decomposition methods (Benders)',
  },
  {
    area: 'Power Systems',
    items:
      'Unit dispatch and storage scheduling, capacity expansion planning, generation interconnection studies, renewable integration (wind, solar, BESS, hydrogen)',
  },
  {
    area: 'Techno-Economic Analysis',
    items: 'NPV and lifecycle cost analysis, LCOE/LCOA, discounted cash flow, sensitivity and scenario analysis',
  },
  { area: 'Languages', items: 'English (native), French (intermediate)' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About David MacKay, energy systems engineer (E.I.T.).">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">Energy systems engineer (E.I.T.) working on power system modelling and optimization.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      I studied Aerospace and Mechanical Engineering at Carleton University. Field work with
      Northern Energy Innovation in the Yukon, mapping remote community power systems from
      generator to load, sparked my move from aerospace into power and energy systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      Today, I'm an Energy Systems E.I.T. at Angler Solutions in St. John's, where I help lead
      development of the optimization module for MESO (Model for Energy Systems
      Optimization). Forecasting wind turbine icing losses and reservoir inflows to inform
      day-ahead bidding has drawn me toward power markets, which is where I want to build my career.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before that, I was a research associate with the APEX Research Group at Carleton, where I
      co-authored a paper on hydrogen microgrids for remote northern communities, published in
      <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2025.126758"><em>Applied Energy</em></a> in 2025.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside work, I plan and lead months-long, self-supported expeditions. They've taught me
      first-hand what risk assessment really means, and they've made me thrive in high-pressure,
      dynamic environments. <a href="/expeditions/">More on that here.</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Skills</h2>
    <dl class="skills">
      {
        skills.map((skill) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{skill.area}</dt>
            <dd>{skill.items}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .skills {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
